Description: Guardian Plane system control/recovery daemon and clients
 Guardian Plane is a privilege-separated system control/recovery plane
 for Ubuntu. This package installs guardian-daemon (unprivileged core
 and monitoring process), guardian-helper (a narrow, polkit-gated
 privileged mutation process), and four read-only D-Bus clients:
 guardian (CLI), guardian-tui, guardian-gui, and guardian-indicator
 (a session tray indicator, autostarted via XDG autostart). No client
 ever runs as root or calls sudo; all privileged mutation is confined
 to guardian-helper behind polkit.
